From 51cced4805038d551440e96b377a6d5823919381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chufleco <80735658+chufleco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:09:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] phy: sunxi-cadence-combophy: enable CMN PLL1 clock on the
 DP+USB path

On the Orange Pi Zero 3W (A733/sun60iw2), USB-C DisplayPort sinks that
also use USB (Type-C pin assignment D: 2-lane DP + USB2) show a black
screen. HPD, EDID and DPCD read fine, but the combophy DP PLL never
reports lock and link training fails at every rate:

  combophy0 dp wait pll enable timeout line:827
  combophy0 dp wait pll enable timeout line:845
  [EDP_ERR]: swing voltage reach max level, training1(clock recovery training) fail!

combo0_dp_set_rate() (the 4-lane DP-only path) enables the CMN PLL1
clock (PHY_PMA_ISO_PLL_CTRL0 cmn_pll1_clk_en, 0xe003 = 0x0003) before the
PLL-enable poll. combo0_configure_usb_dp() never writes it, so on the
DP+USB path the PLL-enable poll in combo0_dp_phy_reset() times out and
no serial clock reaches the lanes.

Add the missing write, matching the DP-only path. With this change
DP-1 trains at 5.4G/2-lane and both a USB-C DP+touch monitor and a plain
USB-C to HDMI adapter display correctly (previously black). DP-only and
USB-only paths are unchanged.

Fixes: https://github.com/orangepi-xunlong/linux-orangepi/issues/133
Signed-off-by: Chufleco <80735658+chufleco@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c b/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
index 94c651e36dc8..4f617c09bb77 100755
--- a/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
@@ -2270,6 +2270,12 @@ static int combo0_configure_usb_dp(struct sunxi_cadence_combophy *combo0)
 		phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0x42EA << 1), 0x00F0);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Enable CMN PLL1 clock (PHY_PMA_ISO_PLL_CTRL0 cmn_pll1_clk_en). The
+	 * DP-only path (combo0_dp_set_rate) writes this before the PLL-enable
+	 * poll; without it the DP PLL never locks on the 2-lane DP+USB path.
+	 */
+	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xe003 << 1), 0x0003);
 	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xE005 << 1), 0x000B);
 	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xE006 << 1), 0x2224);
 	if (combo0->orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE) {
